#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087768 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087585 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/id #uuid "16faff9a-9599-5b8c-85cd-132f3e3f4b92" :question/math-academy-id "e-6150" :question/problem "The circle below is centered at $C(2, 0)$ and the point $X(-1, 4)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle.\n\n![](images/ec/ec8cd56c5a957321de6867c329d53839a924f66714de9941ebb088081680cfbf.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(2-(-1))}^{2}+{(0-4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548268 :question-generator/id #uuid "78cff98a-9f06-5652-9413-1df86fa11866" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186087768.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41966cdb-4ae0-5538-9bc6-e14f91d4170f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330531} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd5e9e5-1f75-55a3-a81f-00682c5cd0dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331201} {:answer/id #uuid "91982f68-5ef2-530b-998a-6c4d449f2b6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331244} {:answer/id #uuid "aa024009-c4d9-5a22-a9e5-fe96f4fb3494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331458} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb27233-f2ce-5f96-b456-6c8d1e14e5c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41966cdb-4ae0-5538-9bc6-e14f91d4170f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330531} :answer-field/id #uuid "859e0875-e943-5c0a-9921-5b1a5dbe9076" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51473619-1294-5307-bfc0-3377a609fc5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-54215" :question/problem "![](images/63/63102dc32e44d75681b95ca5570c737224d7fd887d7c86d2b5c7a1e41a26c9f3.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(4,-4)$ and the point $X(-4,2)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(4-(-4))}^{2}+{(-4-2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y-(-4))^{2} & =(10)^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2} & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id