\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb0ea5e-ad3e-596c-a47f-1b2f569400c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250794} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd34dda-6f93-5397-a33e-2a03884b982c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250807} {:answer/id #uuid "b690d28c-7840-5bec-9fea-01836e32189d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252161} {:answer/id #uuid "bff71f03-a6dd-5c42-a982-4c93c6ea8bd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252249} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbf80d1-3ee1-578b-9627-526049a9423e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b690d28c-7840-5bec-9fea-01836e32189d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252161} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d7781ff-a993-5178-9bac-63ccd91c2ea5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "014cf060-ee36-5cab-a46b-0c5421540a60" :question/math-academy-id "q-117099" :question/problem "![](images/2b/2bd7e3cb9594623c6f5dc3fad35c33c71df0efe9e80b2053dde33f4ef9080bda.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the point $X(0,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(0-(-4))^{2}+(-1-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f70d2a-fc69-5d4c-8d76-eb29f542cee8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339477} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8195c7-e766-5e8a-9057-7cf807388cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340095} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa99c96-03d0-5732-b316-93ca22442393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340366} {:answer/id #uuid "c9082b17-653a-55a6-b4da-3fcc60887456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340909} {:answer/id #uuid "e3377fdf-0433-59b7-872c-aa80d378fdc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f70d2a-fc69-5d4c-8d76-eb29f542cee8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339477} :answer-field/id #uuid "30d50e00-9328-53c1-9634-e13ef473cc3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54aa38dd-d17e-53f7-9a6f-f5bb4a2cb026" :question/math-academy-id "q-72617" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d45a9c753270dfd9186bc16736d1815a11997c88d2f35a0c40f487e6acef66c6.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-2,3)$ and the point $X(1,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-2))}^{2}+{(-1-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341842 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024d17a6-71d7-5b07-a9f7-4e90925b4266" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339148} {:answer/id #uuid "39733cc5-69a1-5e1d-bebb-7bb234749a05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339644} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc3778a-58ce-553d-acdf-2eca8ef39844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340954} {:answer/id #uuid "d77e9864-505e-5fbd-9ca7-87866b380248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341040} {:answer/id #uuid "e5fd184d-c4e9-5208-a605-04a08c3cfd8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5fd184d-c4e9-5208-a605-04a08c3cfd8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341162} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dcfaa52-1bc6-5a58-9c52-332c3dac793a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9071118-1df3-5b01-93dc-2b5f04fcff39" :question/math-academy-id "q-72619" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2ff035f38f5892f61d1eb037c7e39c59c8ec5104babac45224c4902152a0cfaa.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-1,-3)$ and the point $X(1,1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-1))}^{2}+{(1-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{20})^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44ceba2e-461c-5d6f-94d0-fffabcaa7f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339737} {:answer/id #