+(y-0)^{2} & =(5)^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+y^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a098862-af35-5fca-a70c-2ff501c8a7de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}+y^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548200} {:answer/id #uuid "5b16110b-61f1-50e1-ba6c-351866ea0845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+y^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548227} {:answer/id #uuid "74bac309-f6e8-5afb-b8df-f509af5cc748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+11)^{2}+(y-8)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548234} {:answer/id #uuid "d922150d-34f0-53dd-bc8d-0fc5316f1032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+y^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548256} {:answer/id #uuid "df01fd98-356f-5bde-b7a6-d122151caeaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+y^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df01fd98-356f-5bde-b7a6-d122151caeaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+y^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548258} :answer-field/id #uuid "13e72b4a-b73f-5dc7-8505-dbad30c26816" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50f4a650-7500-5a11-b25f-61969e9fc4d0" :question/problem "![](images/61/61afb933b90d96707e44321590837dc4abbfb520ccdc50c3d77ebd930181b9ff.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-5,0)$ and the point $X(-11,8)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(-11-(-5))}^{2}+{(8-0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-5))^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & =(10)^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+y^{2} & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3db882d6-299b-57e2-bf79-64ae8f5ad67e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{41}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548219} {:answer/id #uuid "84261f74-6d85-52e4-8990-c9b734242678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{41}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548242} {:answer/id #uuid "9d6923c4-1ab5-5927-9296-94c1ec43478f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548247} {:answer/id #uuid "a8978ff3-c260-5405-8136-a305f8c97e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548249} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b78d40-1db1-560a-8609-e5217894e2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{41}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84261f74-6d85-52e4-8990-c9b734242678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{5}{2})^{2}=\\frac{41}{2}" :db/id #edb/